SUMMARY:Door 2: Length beats complexity
DESCRIPTION:DO: Use long passphrases and a password manager - one unique pa
 ssword for every account.\nDON’T: Reuse passwords. IT: don’t force sch
 eduled resets - require a change when there’s evidence of compromise.\n\
 nLesson learnt (23andMe\, Oct 2023): Credential stuffing with reused passw
 ords opened about 14\,000 accounts - and\, through a sharing feature\, exp
 osed profile data of about 6.9 million users.\n\nOpen the door: https://aw
 are-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=2\n\nAI-assisted · an init
 iative of ENISA’s ARCH AHWG
