SUMMARY:Door 14: Keys belong in a vault
DESCRIPTION:DO: Keep keys in a secrets manager\, scan every commit\, and re
 view AI-written code like any pull request.\nDON’T: Hard-code tokens or 
 share over-permissive links - or paste keys into an AI assistant to “hel
 p debug”.\n\nLesson learnt (Microsoft AI research\, Sep 2023): A GitHub 
 repo for open AI training data shared an over-permissive storage token\, e
 xposing 38 TB of internal data\, including secrets and private keys.\n\nOp
 en the door: https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=14\n
 \nAI-assisted · an initiative of ENISA’s ARCH AHWG
